---
layout: default
---
{% comment %}
  This page renders the CV from assets/json/resume.json, which follows the JSON Resume
  schema at https://jsonresume.org/schema/. The jekyll-get-json plugin loads that file into
  site.data.resume, and _config.yml points at it under jekyll_get_json.

  Edit assets/json/resume.json to change the CV. The page renders the sections in the order
  the keys appear in that file, so reorder the keys to reorder the page.

  A section appears only when _config.yml lists its key under jsonresume and a matching
  include exists in _includes/resume/. To add a section, write the include, list the key,
  and add a branch to the case statement below.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="post">
  <header class="post-header">
    <h1 class="post-title">
      {{ page.title }}
      {% if page.cv_pdf %}
        <a
          {% if page.cv_pdf contains '://' %}
            href="{{ page.cv_pdf }}"
          {% else %}
            href="{{ page.cv_pdf | prepend: 'assets/pdf/' | relative_url }}"
          {% endif %}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="float-right"
        >
          <i class="fa-solid fa-file-pdf"></i>
        </a>
      {% endif %}
    </h1>
    {% if page.description %}
      <p class="post-description">{{ page.description }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </header>

  <article>
    {% if site.data.resume %}
      <div class="cv">
        {% for data in site.data.resume %}
          {% if site.jsonresume and site.jsonresume.size > 0 %}
            {% unless site.jsonresume contains data[0] %}
              {% continue %}
            {% endunless %}
          {% endif %}
          {% if data[0] == 'meta' or data[1].size == 0 %} {% continue %} {% endif %}
          <a class="anchor" id="{{ data[0] }}"></a>
          <div class="card mt-3 p-3">
            <h3 class="card-title font-weight-medium">{{ data[0] | capitalize }}</h3>
            <div>
              {% case data[0] %}
                {% when 'basics' %}
                  {% include resume/basics.liquid %}
                {% when 'work' %}
                  {% include resume/work.liquid %}
                {% when 'education' %}
                  {% include resume/education.liquid %}
                {% when 'projects' %}
                  {% include resume/projects.liquid %}
                {% when 'presentations' %}
                  {% include resume/presentations.liquid %}
                {% when 'awards' %}
                  {% include resume/awards.liquid %}
                {% when 'certificates' %}
                  {% include resume/certificates.liquid %}
                {% when 'skills' %}
                  {% include resume/skills.liquid %}
                {% when 'publications' %}
                  {% include resume/publications.liquid %}
                {% when 'languages' %}
                  {% include resume/languages.liquid %}
                {% when 'interests' %}
                  {% include resume/interests.liquid %}
                {% when 'volunteer' %}
                  {% include resume/volunteer.liquid %}
                {% when 'references' %}
                  {% include resume/references.liquid %}
                {% else %}

              {% endcase %}
            </div>
          </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    {% else %}
      <p>
        This page found no CV data. Put your CV in <code>assets/json/resume.json</code> in the
        <a href="https://jsonresume.org/schema/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">JSON Resume</a>
        format, and check that <code>jekyll_get_json</code> in <code>_config.yml</code> points at it.
      </p>
    {% endif %}
  </article>
</div>
